          {
            "_key": "a3-17",
            "_type": "span",
            "marks": [],
            "text": "This is the honest counterpoint. If your site’s main job is publishing (a newsroom, a high-volume blog, a team of non-technical editors filing daily), the WordPress dashboard is hard to beat. It’s familiar, and the editing workflow is built for that pace. Sanity is good, and most clients edit from it happily, but it’s a different model. If you need ten or more posts a week from staff who don’t touch code, WordPress makes sense."
          }
        ],
        "markDefs": [],
        "style": "normal"
